// @no-instantiate
// MISCOMPILE, pinned: an UN-ANNOTATED map local (`const c = Map()`) whose value is written
// as an anonymous object literal and which is then handed to a parameter annotated
// `{[string]: Circle}` — a map over a union ARM — in a module that also declares a
// standalone struct of that arm's exact layout (`Dot`). Ten lines, no import, no generic,
// no lambda. `vl check` exits 0 with NO diagnostics at all and is the ONLY command that
// misses it; `vl check --codegen` exits 1, `vl build` writes the `.wasm` and exits 1,
// `vl run` exits 1:
//
//   the emitted module is not valid wasm … type mismatch:
//   expected (ref $type), found (ref $type)
//
// (No byte offset quoted on purpose: it moves with the seed. The message is the stable
// identifier, and the two `$type`s are two DIFFERENT heap types behind one placeholder.)
//
// IT IS A REGRESSION AND THE BISECT NAMES THE COMMIT. This program RAN, printing 7, on
// `6ac49ac9` (#1951, D52) — a seed rebuilt from that commit's own sources, 1,437,150 bytes,
// which reproduces the size that PR reported and is therefore self-verifying. It is
// check-clean invalid wasm on `2ea654d2` (#1952, D48/D63/D64, seed 1,437,704 bytes) and on
// every commit since, `8bf0f20f` included. So #1952's mv find/mint rewrite turned a running
// program silent. Its own 770-cell grid could not see it: that grid had no map-valued
// container, and this is 96 cells of the 9,450-cell D52 grid — `cont=mapval`, every route,
// both declaration orders, and silent on both sides of the change this file ships with.
//
// THE TWIN IS THE AXIS AND IT TURNS A LOUD FLOOR OFF, which is D63's signature one layer
// over. Delete `type Dot` and the same program is the LOUD `emitProgram: only i32, i64, f64,
// f32, boolean, struct, union, array, or string parameters are supported`. ANNOTATE the
// local `: {[string]: Circle}` and it is a DIFFERENT loud floor (`unsupported map value
// type …`), so this is not the annotated-map path — run this file verbatim.
//
// FILED AS `silent-class-inventory.md` D87. NOT FIXED HERE ON PURPOSE: the mv find/mint
// sites are the region #1952 rewrote and the region `D47` (an arm-valued map's inline
// annotation spelling) is open in, so the fix belongs with whoever holds that seam rather
// than bolted onto the struct/variant pin work this file ships beside.
//
// IT IS THE SPECIMEN. This file is kept byte-for-byte identical to
// `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts`'s `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` below its header, which needs a
// program that type-checks clean and whose module the engine refuses.
//
// WHEN IT IS FIXED this file starts failing (the module instantiates), which is the point:
// delete it, graduate a `@run` row, and swap `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` for another live member of
// the class. READ THE NOTE IN `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts` BEFORE DOING THAT — including
// what it says about where to look before concluding the class is empty. Re-running an
// OLDER grid is what found this one: the inventory grades only the rows someone filed.
type Circle = { r: i32 }
type Sq = { s: i32 }
type Shape = Circle | Sq
type Dot = { r: i32 }
function thru(x: {[string]: Circle}) { return x }
function mk(n: i32) {
  const c = Map()
  c["k"] = { r: n }
  return thru(c)
}
print(((mk(7))["k"] ?? { r: 0 }).r)
